{"seq":14,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T17:04:31.042Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0aac979010133d676480d4d599efe49596ce3972a49a5b4965429977c90fca54","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**: Eau Claire dock-door kiosk alerts. Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025. Source: Moss, \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). The action item was to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**: Gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Thea logged it, and it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: Moss, \"North cheat sheet\" (undated).\n\nMoss's other Quarrendon notes (\"Q2/renewal check-in\" from 23 Mar 2026 and \"North pipeline digest\" from 14 Sep 2025) have no ticket numbers.\n\nOne thing to check before you file it: a July 2025 note by Marcus Lindqvist (not Moss) also cites #4419, but describes it as \"Gate 3 printer lag.\" That doesn't match Moss's description of the same number, so it may be a mix-up in the tickets or the notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
